An inner loop records a pair of counters and leaves as soon as its own counter reaches one, and the outer loop leaves when its counter reaches two. What does the printer output?
public class I058 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String log = "";
        int i = 0;
        while (i < 3) {
            int j = 0;
            while (j < 2) {
                log = log + i + "" + j + " ";
                j++;
                if (j == 1) {
                    break;
                }
            }
            i++;
            if (i == 2) {
                break;
            }
        }
        System.out.println(log.trim());
    }
}

A loop adds ten to a counter on every pass and throws on the second pass, which a catch clause inside the loop turns into an extra one. What does the printer output?
public class I059 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int count = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
            try {
                count = count + 10;
                if (i == 1) {
                    throw new IllegalStateException("x");
                }
            } catch (IllegalStateException e) {
                count = count + 1;
            }
        }
        System.out.println(count);
    }
}

A helper records every time it is asked and says whether a value is positive, and the program asks it twice in one condition. Which operator completes the condition so that the second helper is never called?
public class I060 {
    static int calls = 0;
    static boolean check(int v) {
        calls = calls + 1;
        return v > 0;
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        boolean ok = check(0) <<HERE>> check(1);
        System.out.println(ok + ":" + calls);
    }
}
